  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Limited edition of 111 exemplars.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Includes a signed and numberered certificate of authenticity printed on a loose sheet.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">A cardboard with the shape of a bellows binds cover sides which are opposite the spine. When fully open the books unfold into a 10-sided accordion enclosed circle. When fully closed, the pages (issued in a smaller size) take the half left side and the accordion folded sheet takes the half right side.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Hand-bound between CA-Celestina Alessio (Barcelona) and Fa Taller Estudio (Argentina), the edition comprises silkscreen images based on frottages (an artistic technique that involves rubbing a pencil or paper on a surface to create an image) from the sidewalks of Barcelona (Spain) and from the sidewalks of the city of the "diagonals", La Plata (Argentina). This artist's has an interactive square format that allows the viewer to immerse themselves in the book by sticking their head under a fold-out blue accordion piece of paper.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"24 páginas impresas en papel coral, con imágenes basadas en frottages de la verada de el Espacio diagonal (La Plata) y de las aceras de Barcelona"--Page 2 of cover.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="590" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">UNC-CH copy lacks certificate of authenticity.</subfield>
  </datafield>
